summary:
  The logo hunt keeps a picture whose answer Qt's own redirects brought from
  a private host.

history:
  The address is judged before the request, but Qt follows redirects inside
  the network layer: a station page answering "302 to
  http://192.168.1.1/x.png" would hand an internal host's bytes to the
  picture check, and the result would be saved as the station's logo. The
  popup's backfill runs this with no click.

target:
  package/contents/ui/LogoHunt.qml

find:
                  && hunt._fromPublicHost(xhr, strict)) {

replace:
                  && xhr.responseType === "arraybuffer") {

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_the_popup_reads_a_homepage_only_through_the_guarded_hunt,
  which the gate reaches first (unit tests run before the QML tests).
  tests/qml/tst_logohunt.qml::test_a_picture_redirected_into_the_lan_is_not_kept
  goes red on it as well. Line-neutral.
